 style="font-weight:700">Cecily Wellesley-Smith</span><span>&nbsp;(women) at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">FC Roseng&aring;rd</span><span>&nbsp;to Dec 2026; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Tommy Setford</span><span>&nbsp;linked with </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Las Palmas</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. Several senior loans still to be finalised before Sept 1.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="font-weight:700">One to watch:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">Ife Ibrahim</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; singled out alongside </span><span style="font-weight:700">Julienne</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;as the standout of first-team pre-season training.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">ARSENAL WOMEN</span></h2><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Slegers rebuilds: five frees, one fee, and a clear run at September</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">No summer tournament, no Champions League qualifiers, six new senior faces and a seven-week runway to the WSL opener at Brighton. Arsenal Women have not had a pre-season this clean in years.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Ren&eacute;e Slegers</span><span>&nbsp;has had the sort of summer a coach dreams about and rarely gets: a squad rebuilt through the free-agent market, no major international tournament pulling players away, and &mdash; because </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;qualified directly for the Women&#39;s Champions League league phase by finishing second in the WSL &mdash; no August qualifying rounds to disrupt the build-up. As one assessment put it this week, there &quot;looks to be a real chance to hit the ground running.&quot;</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The rebuild was substantial and it was necessary. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Beth Mead</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Katie McCabe</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Manuela Zinsberger</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Laia Codina</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Victoria Pelova</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Naomi Williams</span><span>&nbsp;all left in May. In came five outfield players, four of them on free transfers: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Georgia Stanway</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Bayern Munich</span><span>, filling the defensive-midfield hole left by </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lia W&auml;lti</span><span>; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ona Batlle</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Barcelona</span><span>, a direct answer to </span><span style="font-weight:700">McCabe</span><span>&#39;s departure and capable on either flank; </span><span style="font-weight:700">G&eacute;raldine Reuteler</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Eintracht Frankfurt</span><span>, the most positionally flexible player in the squad; and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Selina Cerci</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Hoffenheim</span><span>, a third forward option behind </span><span style="font-weight:700">Alessia Russo</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Stina Blackstenius</span><span>&nbsp;with 32 goals in 43 Frauen-Bundesliga appearances. The one fee went on </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lisa Baum</span><span>, 19, from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">RB Leipzig</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;for around &pound;510,000 &mdash; the youngest player to score six or more goals in a Bundesliga season.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Baum</span><span>&nbsp;has already justified the outlay. She scored, along with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Chloe Kelly</span><span>, in a 2-1 pre-season win over </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Crystal Palace</span><span>&nbsp;on Saturday &mdash; both goals in the second half. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Frida Maanum</span><span>&nbsp;did not feature; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Steph Catley</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Leah Williamson</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Cerci</span><span>&nbsp;were unavailable, having only recently rejoined full training. The squad then travelled to La Manga for a training camp, with a friendly against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">AC Milan</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;arranged during the trip and a further behind-closed-doors fixture likely.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>Two departures completed the tidying-up. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jenna Nighswonger</span><span>&nbsp;joined NWSL side </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Bay FC</span><span>&nbsp;for a reported &pound;150,000 &mdash; the 25-year-old American made only five competitive appearances after arriving from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Gotham FC</span><span>&nbsp;in January 2025 and spent the second half of last season on loan at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Aston Villa</span><span>, where a purchase option went unexercised. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jessie Gale</span><span>, the young striker, joined </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Newcastle United</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;on loan in WSL2 on August 7.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>The Emirates hosts every WSL home game again this season, for the second year running, with league-phase Champions League and domestic cup ties staying at Meadow Park. Home European football at the Emirates resumes only from the quarter-finals &mdash; should </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;get there.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Arsenal Women &mdash; What&#39;s Next</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Sun Aug 23:</span><span>&nbsp;v </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Paris FC</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; Meadow Park, 1:00pm BST / </span><span style="font-weight:700">5:00am Pacific</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(friendly)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Wed Aug 26:</span><span>&nbsp;v </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Charlton Athletic</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; Meadow Park, 7:00pm BST / </span><span style="font-weight:700">11:00am Pacific</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(friendly)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Sun Sep 6:</span><span>&nbsp;v </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Brighton &amp; Hove Albion</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(a) &mdash; WSL opener</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Europe:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Direct entry to the Women&#39;s Champions League league phase as WSL runners-up</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="font-weight:700">Window:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;WSL summer window closes 11pm, Thursday September 3</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">GUNNERS ABROAD</span></h2><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">A quiet week away &mdash; and a World Cup still being paid for</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">There is no international window this week and no European club football until September. The relevant story abroad is the tournament Arsenal have just come back from.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>For once this section reports an absence rather than a result: there were no competitive international fixtures involving </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;players in the last seven days, and no European club football. The next senior international window opens in early September; the Champions League league phase begins on September 8-10, with the draw at UEFA headquarters in Nyon on Thursday, August 27 at 5pm BST &mdash; 9am Pacific.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The World Cup that finished on July 19 is still the dominant fact of </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s summer. Fifteen players from the title-winning squad went, representing nine nations. Three came back with winners&#39; medals: </span><span style="font-weight:700">David Raya</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mikel Merino</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mart&iacute;n Zubimendi</span><span>, after </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Spain</span><span>&nbsp;beat </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Argentina</span><span>&nbsp;1-0 in extra time through </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ferran Torres</span><span>. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bruno Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>, then still a </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Newcastle</span><span>&nbsp;player, started all five of </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Brazil</span><span>&#39;s matches and provided four assists &mdash; form that is a large part of why </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;paid &pound;75m for him three weeks later. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Saka</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rice</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Eze</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Madueke</span><span>&nbsp;were all in the </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">England</span><span>&nbsp;squad. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Saliba</span><span>&#39;s tournament with </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">France</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;was cut short by the back injury that still has him sidelined.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Among those out on loan and abroad, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Cecily Wellesley-Smith</span><span>&nbsp;continues her spell at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">FC Roseng&aring;rd</span><span>&nbsp;in Sweden through December, and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jessie Gale</span><span>&nbsp;has just begun her loan at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Newcastle United</span><span>&nbsp;in WSL2. </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&#39;s men&#39;s loan list for 2026/27 is still being assembled &mdash; several deals are expected before the September 1 deadline, and we will track each of them here weekly once they are done.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">NUMBERS OF THE WEEK</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">&pound;75m</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; Fee for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bruno Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>: the second-largest in </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s history, with &pound;7m of it owed on to </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Lyon</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">6</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; Goals conceded in </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s two pre-season defeats, to </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Real Betis</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Borussia Dortmund</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&q